00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.200
the holy trifecta, which is the

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:50.360
thumbnail, the title, and the intro.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:51.800
Now, these three things are incredibly

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.440
important and they basically decide

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.400
everything and I highly recommend that

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.840
you do them at the beginning before you

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.200
actually create the video. Now, it's not

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:59.840
only important that you have a good

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.600
thumbnail, title, and intro, but more

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.760
important, it's important that they are

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:05.480
actually congruent with each other. This

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.120
is a mistake that I see people make all

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.960
the time. They might have a 10 out of 10

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:10.360
thumbnail, title, and intro separately,

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.080
but they're not actually congruent with

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.720
each other. And so, it just confuses

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:14.800
people and they click off the video. But

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.280
really, if the thumbnail doesn't get the

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.800
click, nothing else matters. If the

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:19.640
title doesn't match the thumbnail,

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.040
nothing else matters. And if the intro

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.840
doesn't hold the viewer for the first 30

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:25.160
seconds, then nothing else matters. So,

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:26.440
packaging is 70 to 80% of YouTube

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.680
success. So, think of it like a

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.800
restaurant, right? The sign on the

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.560
building is the thumbnail, the menu is

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:33.280
the title, and the first sip of water

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.200
when you sit down is the intro. You want

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:36.280
to get all of these right. If you do

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.040
that, the customer's going to order the

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.400
entire meal. Get any of them wrong, and

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:41.480
they walk out before they ever see the

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:43.160
food, right? If somebody comes in and

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.360
nobody serves them within 10 minutes,

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.600
they're probably going to walk right

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.280
out. And let me give you an example. So,

