00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.120
went through this process. All right, so

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:09.520
step three is the script, and this is

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:11.240
where a lot of creators get destroyed

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:13.480
cuz they just spend way too much time.

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:15.360
And most people sit in front of a blank

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:17.160
document, and they try to write a script

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.840
word for word, and it takes hours,

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:20.640
sometimes days, and then it sounds like

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:22.080
a robot because, well, they basically

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:23.560
just force themselves to write like one,

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:26.000
right? So, here's what I do instead. I

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:27.960
call this the yap-to-script system. And

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:29.920
by the way, I have tried just about

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:32.360
every script writing system out there

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:34.520
known to mankind, and this is by far the

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:36.480
best, okay? So, what you want to do is

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.839
you want to open up some sort of thing

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:39.839
where you're recording yourself. So, it

00:12:37.839 --> 00:12:42.160
could be voice memos on a phone, you

00:12:39.839 --> 00:12:43.760
could be recording directly into an AI.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.240
A lot of them you have the ability to do

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.880
that, but you want to open up something

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:48.240
to record your voice. And then just talk

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:50.760
through the video idea that you have.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:52.440
Now, luckily, with the Claude skill, it

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:54.080
will actually interview you back and

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:55.680
forth, right? So, it's even better

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:57.240
because you can just talk to the Claude

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:58.680
skill, and then it'll just interview you

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.720
back and forth. And you can talk to it

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.760
for 5 minutes just really quickly, or

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.440
you can just go on and on. And

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.520
basically, you just want to yap, right?

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.920
So, you can pretend like you're just

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:08.560
talking to a friend or a partner or a

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:10.320
business buddy or one of your coworkers

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.040
or whatever, right? But basically, just

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.360
go over what you want to talk about in

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.440
the video and the major things that you

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:15.520
want to hit on. And then you drop it

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.520
into the script writer skill, and what

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:18.040
it's going to do is it's going to give

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.320
you an outline, and then it's going to

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:21.200
give you a full script. Now, at this

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:22.760
point, you can obviously modify anything

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.560
that you want. You can go back and forth

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.000
on it, but sometimes it'll nail it on

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:27.680
the first shot. And at this point, you

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.320
also have the ability to choose whether

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.920
you just want to go off of the outline.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.040
Some people prefer that. They just look

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:33.680
at the outline and then they kind of

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.200
just talk off the top of their head. Or

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:36.560
if you want to go word for word off of

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.840
the script. Or there's kind of an

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.560
in-between where you sometimes choose to

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:41.960
use the script and go word for word,

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:43.120
then sometimes you just kind of talk off

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.480
the top of your head. That's sort of

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:45.640
what I do to be completely honest with

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.000
you. But sometimes I'll just use an

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.200
outline and it really just depends on

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.920
the type of video I'm making. Some

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.560
people also prefer to make like a

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:52.960
PowerPoint and then just talk off of the

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:54.200
PowerPoint. But the important thing is

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.560
if you tell the Claude skill what you

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.640
want to do, it'll do it for you. So you

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.240
can kind of think of it like cooking,

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.520
right? You're the chef, you know the

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:02.120
flavors, but you're terrible at writing

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:03.640
recipes down so that anyone else can

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.720
follow them. Claude is the recipe

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:07.200
writer. You taste, you direct, Claude

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.520
organizes. And here's another meta

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.120
moment. The information you're reading

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:12.160
on this video came from a yap session.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.680
Now, to be fair, I do go off the cuff. I

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.440
kind of talk about other stuff, anything

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.920
that pops into my head. I'm a bit ADHD,

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:19.360
so honestly I like to do that. But for

